From 765d138385a1294c668bea0a6e62ac5692b5b267 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bare <git@barebrowser.org>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 08:22:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep toolbar shortcuts current, and stop offering Translate

Shortcuts placed on the toolbar were often greyed out: Share and Translate on
a page that plainly had something to share. BareButtonDataActionAdapter asked
the button's provider whether it could be pressed only when the visible tab
changed. A tab that opened on the new tab page, where Share has nothing to
offer, kept that answer after navigating to an ordinary page, until the user
happened to switch tabs. Measured on a Pixel 3: after navigating such a tab to
example.org both buttons were disabled; switching to another tab on the same
site enabled them at once. The adapter now asks again when the tab's URL
changes.

Translate goes from the choices altogether. It needs a Google API key, which
this build does not have, so even an enabled Translate button could not
translate anything. A slot an earlier release let someone set to Translate
falls back to its default, and a hold set to it does nothing, through the
checks that already discard actions a build no longer offers. Upstream's own
address bar shortcut settings offered it too: AdaptiveToolbarFeatures now
reports Translate as unavailable, so that screen, the shortcut predictor and
the button no longer offer it, and its tests expect that.
